// The waitlist ticket, from the user's Figma export (Frame 15917.svg, 2026-10-02: "this is svg
// we have to use"). The artwork is unchanged apart from three things, each for a reason:
//
//   · SPLIT INTO ITS TWO OBJECTS, the black holder and the gold ticket, because the ticket is the
//     thing that moves (it slides out of the holder when someone joins).
//   · THE GRAIN IS PROCEDURAL. Figma embedded it as a 1024px noise PNG (1.6 MB of a 2.2 MB file);
//     feTurbulence draws the same uniform grain for nothing, as public/site's earlier export did.
//   · THE PRINT IS ADDED: the name, the number and the address, struck in with the logo's emboss
//     in a deeper gold, laid along the same axis, so the light runs through them too. On the BACK
//     the face and grain paths keep only their outline: the export cuts the lockup out of the face
//     as holes, which the front's lockup fills and the back would show as a black wordmark. And a BACK: the same ticket with the mark alone.
//
// Ids are namespaced `zb-` and re-namespaced per instance by the component, so two tickets on one
// page never resolve to each other's gradients.
//
// THE SHINE IS NOT AN OVERLAY. It is where the gold gradients sit. GOLD lists every gradient that
// paints gold (face, border, each logo glyph, the print); sliding them together along SHINE_AXIS
// moves the real shine across the whole ticket at once.

